1. Proxmox console (mini PC screen and keyboard, logged in as root)
nano /etc/network/interfaces

In the vmbr0 section, set these two lines, then save with Ctrl+O, Enter, Ctrl+X:

address 192.168.1.50/24
gateway 192.168.1.254

Then:

nano /etc/hosts

Change only the IP at the start of your host’s line to 192.168.1.50, then save and exit.

reboot
2. Proxmox console: check addresses
ip a
pct list
pct exec 100 ip a
pct exec 101 ip a
3. Proxmox console: Tailscale remote access
echo 'net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1' >> /etc/sysctl.d/99-tailscale.conf
sysctl -p /etc/sysctl.d/99-tailscale.conf
tailscale up --advertise-routes=192.168.1.0/24

Then approve the route at login.tailscale.com > Machines > Proxmox machine > Edit route settings.

4. Windows PowerShell (run as Administrator): make the names work on your laptop

Run this once only:

Add-Content C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts "192.168.1.80 truenas.jprivateproptery.com vault.jprivateproptery.com nginx.jprivateproptery.com"
ipconfig /flushdns
ping vault.jprivateproptery.com

The ping should show 192.168.1.80.

